> 20070503 11:47:30| Normalizing data towards target distribution...done
> 20070503 11:47:30|Quantile normalizing data set...done

I suspect there is a problem print()-ing one of the CEL files when you
use verbose.  The reason why it looks like it is "done", is because
there is a fallback in all methods that always "closes" the indented
verbose message (it is on my wishlist to report "error" instead of
"done", but that is tricky to automate).

Could you please try to do the following:

> ...
> cs <- AffymetrixCelSet$fromName(name, chipType=chipType)
> lapply(cs, print)

and see if you get an error already there?  If you do, then we're on
the right track.  If so, select the/an array that gives you an error,
say the first one, and do:

> cf <- getFile(cs, 1)
> print(cf)

You should see the error again.  For each of the following, tell me
what you get:

> getName(cf)
> getTags(cf)
> getPathname(cf)
> getFileSize(cf)
> objectSize(cf)
> cdf <- getCdf(cf)
> cdf
> getChipType(cdf)
> ts <- getTimestamp(cf)
> ts
> as.character(ts)

/Henrik

