Hi.

Just wondering how I might get the same expression summaries from
'rma' (affy) as 'RmaPlm' (aroma.affymetrix).  My first attempt at this
failed, on a U133 dataset.  I read in the documentation that there are
different options for RmaPlm ('flavour=affyPLM' is favoured).

They are close at high expression, so I wonder if this is a background
correction thing.
http://bioinf.wehi.edu.au/folders/mrobinson/aroma/rma.vs.RmaPlm.png

# -------- for RmaPlm
chip1<- "HG-U133_Plus_2"
cs1 <- AffymetrixCelSet$fromName(name, chipType=chip1)
qn1 <- QuantileNormalization(cs1, typesToUpdate="pm")
csN1 <- process(qn1, verbose=verbose) #time required
plm1.merge <- RmaPlm(csN1)
fit(plm1.merge, verbose=verbose) #time required
chp1.merge<-getChipEffectSet(plm1.merge)
.... getUnits ...

# -------- for justRMA
u133.rma<-justRMA(filenames=fn.u133,celfile.path=".")
d<-exprs(u133.rma)

Thanks,
Mark

